### 1) Login on users-service (port 5001). Use any existing account.
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "hana@example.com", "password": "YOUR_PASSWORD" }

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 2) Health of the new service (public, expect 200 "UP" or "DOWN" if RabbitMQ is off)
GET http://localhost:5002/actuator/health

### 3) Token from users-service is accepted here (expect 200 with userId and role)
GET http://localhost:5002/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4) No token (expect 401, application/problem+json)
GET http://localhost:5002/whoami

### 5) Tampered token (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:5002/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}x

### 6) Admin area with a customer token (expect 403)
GET http://localhost:5002/admin/restaurants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7) Public area needs no token (expect 404 for now: the endpoint doesn't exist yet, but NOT 401)
GET http://localhost:5002/restaurants